  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe turning page family of #1122 draws through the form seam. After the holes family (#1724), this is the second family.\n\n- The family is `turning_page.rs`, `turning_more_page.rs`, `turning_start_exit_rows.rs` and `thread_infeed_page.rs` (the infeed rows of the Threading page). The lathe tool pages (`tool_body_lathe_page.rs`, `tool_turning_row.rs`) are in the tools and machine family, so they are not in this PR.\n- On `main` the family had three raw calls. Each goes through the helper that the holes family added:\n  - the Threading page's Hand row: `ui.radio_value` x 2 becomes `radio_pair`, as on the thread milling page;\n  - the Spring passes row: `ui.add_sized(DragValue)` becomes `fields::int_range_row`, as on the thread milling page. The field now has the row's accessible name (\"Spring passes\") and the house focus ring.\n- The raw-call guard (`layout/form_seam_tests.rs`) gets a `turning` family at 0. The test that pinned the guard to the holes family only (`form_seam_guard_covers_only_the_migrated_holes_family`) now pins the list of migrated families (`form_seam_guard_covers_only_the_migrated_families`). The `#[test]` count stays the same for that file and goes up by one in `thread_hand_tests.rs`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1122-form-seam-turning.md`.\n\nBehaviour-neutral: the same values go into the page draft, and Apply still rides `EditOperationParams`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::layout::form_seam_tests::pages_do_not_add_raw_egui_calls_outside_the_form_seam`: the turning family has 0 raw calls.\n- `egui_app::layout::form_seam_tests::form_seam_guard_covers_only_the_migrated_families`: the guard lists holes and turning, each at 0, with their files.\n- `egui_app::thread_hand_tests::the_spring_passes_field_is_named_by_its_row` (new): the Spring passes number field has the accessible name \"Spring passes\" from its row. Red on `main` (the old `add_sized` field had no name), green after.\n- Also green: `thread_hand_tests` (4 more, including the Hand pick that applies and undoes), `turning_start_exit_rows` (4), `thread_mill_page_tests` (4), `structural::thread_repeat`, and the other `form_seam_tests` (5).\n\nNo new test binary (#3187): the tests are in the `camcraft-ui` lib.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe Threading page's Passes tab (the infeed rows, Spring passes and Hand), from the off-screen renderer (`egui_kittest` with the headless wgpu device) at 620 x 1400, cropped to the top 470 px. A pixel comparison of the full frames gives 0 different pixels: `int_range_row` draws the field at the same size. The images are on the images-only `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork.\n\n| Before (`main` 773736856) | After (42ca7bfc5) |\n|---|---|\n| ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1122-turning/before-threading-passes.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1122-turning/after-threading-passes.png) |\n\n## Gates\n\nOn 42ca7bfc5 (branched from `upstream/main` 773736856):\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (3.4 min). It includes `ui suites: lib`.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-ui -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: the diff reaches none.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI window.\n\nChangelog: none (no behaviour change; the turning Spring passes field gets its row's accessible name).\n\nRefs #1122\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
